# 🎯 4. The Goals of a Data Engineer

The main objectives of data engineering are business-oriented.

## 💰 1. Maximize Return on Investment (ROI)

Data engineers help organizations obtain measurable value from their data infrastructure.

Examples:

- Reducing reporting time
- Improving forecasting
- Automating manual processes
- Reducing operational waste
- Supporting new data products
- Improving decision-making

The full cost of a data solution includes infrastructure, engineering time, maintenance, monitoring, and operational complexity.

## 🛡️ 2. Reduce Risk

Risks include:

- Data breaches
- Incorrect business reporting
- Pipeline failures
- Data loss
- Compliance violations
- Unreliable machine-learning inputs

Security, testing, monitoring, and governance help reduce these risks.

## 📈 3. Maximize the Value of Data

The goal is not to collect the largest possible amount of data.

It is to deliver the right data, with the right quality and availability, to the right consumers, at the right time.

